## Materials Division Safety Deep Dive

**Presenter:** Sarah Chen, Materials EHS Director

### Incident Analysis

| Incident Type | Count | % of Total |
|---------------|-------|------------|
| Ergonomic/Strain | 5 | 42% |
| Chemical Exposure | 3 | 25% |
| Laceration | 2 | 17% |
| Slip/Trip/Fall | 2 | 17% |

### Root Causes Identified

1. **Ergonomic Issues:**
   - Manual material handling in composite layup
   - Repetitive motion in quality inspection
   - Inadequate job rotation

2. **Chemical Exposure:**
   - Ventilation insufficiency in curing area
   - PPE compliance gaps on night shift
   - Training gaps for new materials

### Corrective Actions

| Action | Status | Investment | Completion |
|--------|--------|------------|------------|
| Automated material handling | In Progress | $1.2M | Q2 2026 |
| Ventilation upgrade | Approved | $850K | Mar 2026 |
| Enhanced PPE program | Complete | $120K | Done |
| Night shift supervision | In Progress | $180K/yr | Feb 2026 |
| Ergonomic assessment | Complete | $45K | Done |

