## Serious Incident Review

### Incident #SI-2025-042 (December 2, 2025)

**Location:** Albuquerque Manufacturing Facility
**Type:** Chemical Exposure
**Severity:** OSHA Recordable (Restricted Work)

**Description:**
Employee exposed to epoxy vapors during unplanned venting of curing oven. Employee experienced respiratory irritation and was placed on restricted duty for 5 days.

**Root Cause:**
- Exhaust fan failure not detected
- Sensor alarm was in maintenance mode
- Supervisor signed off on work without verification

**Corrective Actions:**

| Action | Owner | Status |
|--------|-------|--------|
| Replace exhaust fan | Facilities | Complete |
| Install redundant sensor | Engineering | Feb 15 |
| Revise lockout procedure | Safety | Complete |
| Supervisor retraining | HR | Complete |
| Discipline per policy | HR | Complete |

**Lessons Learned:**
- Distributed to all manufacturing sites
- Added to safety training curriculum
- Policy updated to require dual verification

